  "title": "Great room — compact plan (v2)",
  "units": "meters",
  "provenance": {
    "method": "revision of great-room.json after the v1 plan read as too long",
    "source_views": 5,
    "scale_anchor": "standard fixture sizes: 0.92 m counter, 2.03 m door leaf, 0.91 m fridge, 0.66 m barstool seat, 2.74 m ceiling",
    "accuracy": "hypothesis. Differs from v1 in one structural claim, not in measurement.",
    "what_changed": [
      "The media console moves off the east window wall onto a return wall - the dining nook's south face - looking back into the living room.",
      "Footprint drops from 6.30 x 10.60 m to 5.90 x 8.60 m (-2.0 m of depth, -24% floor area).",
      "The empty 3 m band between living room and kitchen is gone; zones now abut.",
      "Everything else - the kitchen L, the nook, the stair on the west wall, the window/door order on the east wall - is unchanged from v1."
    ],
    "why": [
      "v1 required the east wall to carry, in one run: three living-room windows, the French door, a 1.98 m console, and the dining window - plus a nook needing 2.6 m of depth beyond the console. That forces ~10.6 m of depth and leaves a dead band in the middle.",
      "No photo shows a dead band. From the island you see dining table, console, door and living room together, which means the zones are close, not strung out.",
      "Removing the console from that wall frees ~2.5 m of it, which is exactly the depth the room needed to lose."
    ],
    "unresolved": [
      "Whether the console faces south off the nook wall (this plan) or west off the window wall (v1) is not settled by anything I can measure without the source files. View 01 shows console and door together; whether they are coplanar or on a corner turn is the whole question.",
      "Two ceiling fans still assumed, as in v1.",
      "Nook is 2.50 x 2.90 m, which is snug for a 1.07 m round table plus four chairs - consistent with how tight view 05 looks, but at the edge of workable."
    ]
  },
